      "id": 2,
      "text": "George Rogers Clark marched through Walnut Hill in February 1779 on his campaign from Fort Kaskaskia to Fort Vincennes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Hill%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Walnut Hill sat at the crossroads of the historic George Rogers Clark Trace and the Yadda Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Hill%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village lies on the old Goshen Road, an early Illinois route from Shawneetown to Glen Carbon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Hill%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Remnants of the Goshen Road can still be seen in short segments of Pioneer Road between Dix and Walnut Hill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Hill%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
